WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.333


2
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:38.875
<b>At the end of the first chapter,</b>
<b>Arjuna Vishada Yoga,</b>

3
00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:43.916
<b>how Arjuna abandoned his</b>
<b>Gandiva bow and arrows.</b>

4
00:00:43.916 --> 00:00:45.083
<b>He is distressed,</b>

5
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:46.500
<b>sorrowful.</b>

6
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.666
<b>Here in the second chapter,</b>
<b>Lord Krishna will now speak to Arjuna,</b>

7
00:00:51.666 --> 00:00:52.375
<b>and</b>

8
00:00:52.375 --> 00:00:58.375
<b>this is where the teachings of</b>
<b>Lord Krishna will gradually begin</b>

9
00:00:58.375 --> 00:01:05.041
<b>that great wisdom of the Gita which has been</b>
<b>guiding humanity for centuries</b>

10
00:01:05.041 --> 00:01:07.916
<b>In this first verse of the second chapter, </b>

11
00:01:07.916 --> 00:01:10.625
<b>Sanjaya tells Dhritarashtra:</b>

12
00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:13.250
<b>Arjuna was filled with compassion,</b>

13
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.875
<b>his eyes were flowing with tears.</b>

14
00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.958
<b>Seeing him in such a grief-stricken state</b>

15
00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:23.541
<b>Madhusudana Sri Krishna began to speak.</b>

16
00:01:24.208 --> 00:01:28.458


17
00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:31.375
<b>When Arjuna had laid down his weapons, </b>

18
00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:36.583
<b>Dhritarashtra thought that perhaps</b>
<b>he would abandon the war altogether,</b>

19
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:37.958
<b>and if that happened,</b>

20
00:01:37.958 --> 00:01:41.916
<b>victory would surely belong to</b>
<b>his son Duryodhana.</b>

21
00:01:41.916 --> 00:01:42.791
<b>But here,</b>

22
00:01:42.791 --> 00:01:47.291
<b>Sanjaya attempts to dispel</b>
<b>that doubt of Dhritarashtra.</b>

23
00:01:47.291 --> 00:01:48.375
<b>Here, Sanjaya</b>

24
00:01:48.375 --> 00:01:52.083
<b>addresses Sri Krishna as Madhusudana.</b>

25
00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:53.208
<b>Madhusudana </b>

26
00:01:53.208 --> 00:01:56.125
<b>He who slew the demon named Madhu.</b>

27
00:01:56.125 --> 00:01:57.958
<b>It's as if Sanjaya is saying,</b>

28
00:01:57.958 --> 00:01:59.666
<b>"O King Dhritarashtra,</b>

29
00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:02.541
<b>Madhusudana is with Arjuna,</b>

30
00:02:02.541 --> 00:02:07.250
<b>and just as He ended the</b>
<b>life of the demon Madhu,</b>

31
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.500
<b>so too</b>

32
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:15.500
<b>will He swiftly end this dilemma, </b>
<b>this sorrow of Arjuna."</b>

33
00:02:16.166 --> 00:02:20.416


34
00:02:20.416 --> 00:02:24.666
<b>Arjuna is now filled with compassion;</b>

35
00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:28.291
<b>he feels pity even for those</b>

36
00:02:28.291 --> 00:02:34.583
<b>who have done nothing but</b>
<b>deceit and treachery to him.</b>

37
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:40.041
<b>Nothing but unrighteousness.</b>

38
00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:43.583
<b>Is such compassion, right?</b>

39
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:49.250
<b>Are these people even deserving of this pity?</b>

40
00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.333
<b>Pity,</b>

41
00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:51.416
<b> compassion,</b>

42
00:02:51.416 --> 00:02:52.541
<b>empathy</b>

43
00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:54.000
<b>are good values,</b>

44
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.500
<b>essential in life.</b>

45
00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.916
<b>But</b>

46
00:02:58.916 --> 00:03:05.541
<b>the right circumstances for</b>
<b>their use are equally necessary.</b>

47
00:03:05.541 --> 00:03:06.708
<b>Just as</b>

48
00:03:06.708 --> 00:03:12.750
<b>excessive consumption of</b>
<b>sweets can lead to ill health,</b>

49
00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:20.333
<b>too much compassion is also not right.</b>

50
00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.625
<b>If you show mercy towards a harmful pest,</b>

51
00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:27.000
<b>it will destroy the entire crop.</b>

52
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:34.375
<b>What will happen if you repeatedly forgive</b>
<b>an unrighteous person out of empathy?</b>

53
00:03:34.375 --> 00:03:37.250
<b>Unrighteousness will spread further in the world.</b>

54
00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.583
<b>Many more people will suffer from their sins.</b>

55
00:03:40.583 --> 00:03:41.916
<b>So then,</b>

56
00:03:41.916 --> 00:03:48.833
<b>how to know the right use of</b>
<b>pity, compassion, empathy?</b>

57
00:03:48.833 --> 00:03:54.375
<b>By understanding the difference between</b>
<b>material and spiritual foundations.</b>

58
00:03:54.375 --> 00:03:57.416
<b>As long as our thinking is worldly,</b>

59
00:03:57.416 --> 00:04:03.375
<b>and we understand ourselves</b>
<b>only as a body form, a physical form,</b>

60
00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:10.333
<b>our pity and compassion will also</b>
<b>go only towards materiality.</b>

61
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:11.166
<b>But </b>

62
00:04:11.166 --> 00:04:15.458
<b>when we see from a spiritual perspective,</b>

63
00:04:15.458 --> 00:04:20.291
<b>we will move towards human upliftment.</b>

64
00:04:20.291 --> 00:04:27.125
<b>And this Gita will strengthen this very</b>
<b>spiritual perspective of yours.</b>

65
00:04:27.625 --> 00:04:32.000


66
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.875
<b>Generally,</b>

67
00:04:33.875 --> 00:04:39.250
<b>no one openly shows their inner pain.</b>

68
00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:43.666
<b>Everyone tries to portray that all is well,</b>

69
00:04:43.666 --> 00:04:48.500
<b>the situation is under control, they are strong.</b>

70
00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.208
<b>We fear</b>

71
00:04:50.208 --> 00:04:53.791
<b>that someone might consider us weak.</b>

72
00:04:53.791 --> 00:05:01.083
<b>We don't even let people sense the storm</b>

73
00:05:01.083 --> 00:05:02.625
<b>But</b>

74
00:05:02.625 --> 00:05:04.500
<b> you know,</b>

75
00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.208
<b>this isn't entirely true.</b>

76
00:05:08.208 --> 00:05:10.958
<b>Doubts and dilemmas of the mind</b>

77
00:05:10.958 --> 00:05:13.833
<b>are natural for humans.</b>

78
00:05:13.833 --> 00:05:16.250
<b>To some extent, it's also natural</b>

79
00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:23.625
<b>that we hide our state of mind</b>
<b>from those who cannot help us.</b>

80
00:05:23.625 --> 00:05:25.375
<b>However,</b>

81
00:05:25.375 --> 00:05:28.625
<b>a big mistake occurs</b>

82
00:05:28.625 --> 00:05:38.000
<b>when we start hiding our true state of mind</b>
<b>from our loved ones, from our well-wishers.</b>

83
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:44.583
<b>Suppressing the mind like this starts</b>
<b>to hollow us out like termites,</b>

84
00:05:44.583 --> 00:05:46.625
<b>and in this hollowness,</b>

85
00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:50.916
<b>mental illnesses find their home.</b>

86
00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:54.208
<b>Arjuna too is a great warrior.</b>

87
00:05:54.208 --> 00:05:59.708
<b>Who could be stronger and</b>
<b>more confident than him,</b>

88
00:05:59.708 --> 00:06:01.083
<b>but</b>

89
00:06:01.083 --> 00:06:09.375
<b>but in this situation, he's openly expressing</b>
<b>his anguish before me, before his Krishna.</b>

90
00:06:09.375 --> 00:06:11.291
<b>Because he knows</b>

91
00:06:11.291 --> 00:06:16.916
<b>that openly sharing one's dilemma at</b>
<b>the right place and with the right person</b>

92
00:06:16.916 --> 00:06:23.083
<b>is not a sign of weakness,</b>
<b>but of strength and harmony.</b>

93
00:06:23.083 --> 00:06:29.083
<b>What shame is there in sharing the mind's</b>
<b>dilemma with a loved one?</b>

94
00:06:29.083 --> 00:06:30.625
<b>You too, recognize</b>

95
00:06:30.625 --> 00:06:35.083
<b>those family members who</b>
<b>can give you impartial advice,</b>

96
00:06:35.083 --> 00:06:36.000
<b>or at </b>

97
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.416
<b>least listen to you with purity and empathy.</b>

98
00:06:41.416 --> 00:06:45.250
<b>By sharing, the storm in the mind calms down,</b>

99
00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:48.250
<b>the dust flying before the eyes clears,</b>

100
00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:52.208
<b>the path starts to appear clear,</b>

101
00:06:52.208 --> 00:06:57.541
<b>and the relationship with that person</b>
<b>also becomes stronger.</b>

102
00:06:57.541 --> 00:06:59.375
<b>Think about it.</b>

103
00:06:59.875 --> 00:07:04.083


104
00:07:04.083 --> 00:07:06.208
<b>Whether it's personal life</b>

105
00:07:06.208 --> 00:07:08.291
<b>or professional,</b>

106
00:07:08.291 --> 00:07:12.291
<b>emotions are an integral part of life.</b>

107
00:07:12.291 --> 00:07:18.333
<b>Only a machine can be</b>
<b>completely devoid of them,</b>

108
00:07:18.333 --> 00:07:20.333
<b>not a human.</b>

109
00:07:20.333 --> 00:07:21.583
<b>But</b>

110
00:07:21.583 --> 00:07:28.125
<b>emotions should be gentle like a breeze,</b>

111
00:07:28.125 --> 00:07:29.208
<b>because</b>

112
00:07:29.208 --> 00:07:32.750
<b>if their storm becomes too intense,</b>

113
00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:35.583
<b>the dust of emotions</b>

114
00:07:35.583 --> 00:07:39.791
<b>will make everything appear</b>
<b>hazy to the mind's eye.</b>

115
00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:44.750
<b>Neither logic nor the right path will be visible.</b>

116
00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:49.583
<b>And it's crucial for the mind's eye to see clearly.</b>

117
00:07:49.583 --> 00:07:56.791
<b>Even the world's most successful individuals</b>
<b>first clearly saw their success in their minds, </b>

118
00:07:56.791 --> 00:08:01.833
<b>only then were they able to bring it into reality.</b>

119
00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:04.125
<b>To do this, one needs</b>

120
00:08:04.125 --> 00:08:09.458
<b>a balance between mental peace</b>
<b>and the power of reasoning.</b>

121
00:08:09.458 --> 00:08:11.166
<b>Mental peace</b>

122
00:08:11.166 --> 00:08:13.333
<b>will illuminate the path,</b>

123
00:08:13.333 --> 00:08:17.791
<b>and reason will give the strength to walk on it.</b>

124
00:08:17.791 --> 00:08:23.375
<b>Maintain a balance of</b>
<b>both for professional success.</b>

125
00:08:23.375 --> 00:08:29.458
<b>You must be continuously</b>
<b>strengthening your work efficiency;</b>

126
00:08:29.458 --> 00:08:36.291
<b>keep your state of mind strong as well with</b>
<b>the power of spiritual knowledge.</b>

